/*
:name: matched_filter_1
:type: lec
:set: compile.upass.roll_arrays=true
:expect_instances: u_loop_0=1 u_loop_1=1 u_loop_2=1 u_loop_3=1 t=1
:lec_grep: roll declined for `for lvl`: a loop nested in the body has a domain that reads the index
*/
// The base design with ARRAY carries allowed to roll (`compile.upass.roll_arrays=true`):
// the tap chain and each of the LOG2N=3 per-level node loops become ONE
// replicated Sub each — `:expect_instances:` pins that — LEC'd against the
// base, which under the default (`compile.unroll=false`, roll_arrays=false)
// declines every loop of this design ("`v` is an array carried across the
// lifted boundary") and is therefore one instance per iteration (15 Subs).
//
// The `:lec_grep:` pins the one loop that must NOT roll even then: the level
// loop's body holds the node loop whose domain `N >> (lvl + 1)` reads `lvl` —
// a runtime port inside a lifted body — so it unrolls and each of its three
// copies rolls the inner loop with a constant count (4, 2, 1).
//
// STATUS 2026-08-22: the rolled form is correct through Verilog emission
// (Icarus reproduces the golden signature bit for bit) and `lhd lec` proves
// rolled == unrolled for every sub-shape tried (taps only, comb levels,
// stateful callee + scalar carry, stateful output into a lane), but on the
// full design `lhd lec` reports a divergence at the LAST checked step with
// all-zero inputs (rolled vs the golden .v) or only a bounded pass (rolled vs
// unrolled) — an encoder artifact of registers inside materialized
// occurrences still to be run down. Until then this pair may be RED; that is
// the claim, not a reason to tag it.
